<main id="content" class="site-main post mt-article"><div class="page-header"><h1 class="entry-title">Design Considerations for Water Features In Commercial Buildings</h1></div><div class="page-content"><p class="mt-article-meta"><time datetime="2023-09-07T15:01:00">September 7, 2023</time></p><figure class="mt-article-hero"><img src="/wp-content/uploads/ALTER-26.jpg" srcset="/wp-content/uploads/ALTER-26-100x100.jpg 100w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-26.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-26-150x145.jpg 150w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-26-300x290.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-26-380x367.jpg 380w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-26-480x464.jpg 480w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-26.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px" width="600" height="580" alt="Design Considerations for Water Features In Commercial Buildings" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></figure><div class="mt-article-body">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We all have been in awe at some point in our lives when we witness captivating water features in a building. Such experiences are what it’s all about for commercial buildings. There is no denying that water features can add a touch of luxury and sophistication to any commercial building. In addition to that, they can also help to improve air quality, reduce stress levels, and create a more inviting and relaxing environment for employees and customers alike.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">However, when designing a water feature for a commercial building, there are a number of factors to consider to ensure your building gets the most out of any water feature, be it a <a href="/rain-curtains/">rain curtain</a>, indoor water fountain, or bubble wall. In this blog, we will be discussing design considerations for water features when installing them in commercial buildings. Let’s begin.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>1. Location.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One of the most important factors to consider when designing a water feature is its location. The water feature should be placed in a prominent location where it can be easily seen and enjoyed by everyone in the building. It should also be placed in a location where it will not be in the way of traffic or cause any safety hazards.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>2. Size.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The size of the water feature should be proportional to the size of the space. A water feature that is too large or too small will look out of place. It is important to choose a water feature that is the right size for the space, and that will complement the overall design of the building.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>3. Type.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There are a variety of different types of water features available, including fountains, bubble tubes, water walls, and streams. The type of water feature you choose will depend on the desired aesthetic and the budget.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>4. Materials.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The materials used to construct the water feature should be durable and able to withstand the elements. Some popular materials for water features include concrete, stone, and stainless steel.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>5. Lighting.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Lighting can be used to enhance the beauty of a water feature at night. There are a variety of different types of lighting available, including underwater lighting, landscape lighting, and accent lighting.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>How Midwest Tropical Can Help With Custom Water Features.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Since 1977, Midwest Tropical has designed and installed custom water features in all 50 states and internationally. We offer a wide variety of water features, including rain curtains, water walls, <a href="/materials/glass-water-features/">water bubble</a> features, and more. We can also work with you to create a custom water feature that perfectly meets your needs and budget.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Here’s What You Get at Midwest Tropical!</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We have a team of experienced and knowledgeable designers who can help you create the perfect water feature for your commercial building. We offer a wide variety of water features to choose from, so you can find the perfect water feature for your needs and budget. We use only the highest quality materials and construction methods to ensure that your water feature will last for years to come. Moreover, we provide comprehensive maintenance and support services to keep your water feature looking and functioning at its best.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you are interested in adding a custom water feature to your commercial building, please contact Midwest Tropical today. We would be happy to discuss your needs and help you create the perfect water feature for your space.</p>



